  "authored_scope": "Supported: output always 3x4. Input canvas 6..30 per side (random default 8..16). 2..6 random pieces (default 2..5) and 2..8 explicit regions. Partitions are drawn by an anchored random sampler that guarantees exactly k regions; a randomized exhaustive partition DFS is the fallback. Same-colour reuse is allowed for congruent, non-touching pieces. Base proposals are unrotated (cost 0) and are then perturbed by rotating 1-2 pieces. Rotation-preference swap ties use the left-piece convention. Preference-critical scenes require a costlier tiling with a different painted grid. An exact gap-respecting packer handles tight canvases, including 6 pieces on 6x6. Explicit latent arguments reconstruct all canonical fixtures. Deliberately not supported: position ties (decided by an undemonstrated reading-order rule), mirrored pieces, ambiguous minimum-cost outputs, same-colour reuse between non-congruent pieces in random scenes, and same-colour regions touching on the board.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Regions partition the 3x4 board into 4-connected pieces; translated copies never touch on the board.",
    "Translated copies share a colour; adjacent board regions always differ in colour; random scenes reuse a colour only among congruent pieces.",
    "The constructed tiling has minimum rotation count, and every minimum-cost tiling paints the same grid, except the demonstrated swap tie, which the constructed grid wins.",
    "In swap-tie scenes the unrotated winner lies entirely left of its rival in the input.",
    "Pieces in the input never overlap and keep an empty cell between them, diagonals included; this is enforced exactly by disjoint 2x2-fattened shapes.",
    "The critical flag means some strictly costlier tiling paints a different output grid; same-colour rearrangements that keep the grid do not count.",
    "The fixed-scene critical precheck uses the actual colours and runs only when colours are supplied.",
    "Explicit tie/critical flags are strict; default preferences are soft and are dropped after half the attempts and in the fallback DFS.",
    "Malformed explicit arguments (wrong containers, lengths, types, ranges) raise ValueError."
  ],
